# Proposed by the executor of F68 (2026-10-15), from what a second reading of the code found; the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: rules that give room unasked ("too little left over is nothing", "squeezed by nobody") are about what Arbor found, never about
# what a hand has made since. And whoever is away when it leaves for good has lent its room already: no column opens under whoever is there.
# Reference: F68, F61.
quiet
# Mail took what was left, a half. Its person drags it down to a tile. Looking around brings no share back.
open Safari 900x600
open Mail 900x600
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
resize 102 left -560
expect tile 102
expect size 101 1262x851
zoom 101
show-all
expect tile 102
expect size 101 1262x851
close 101
close 102

# Squeezed against the Desktop a window is as narrow as its person wants it.
open Safari 800x600 min 500x300
dock 103 left
resize 103 right -400
expect tile 103
zoom 103
show-all
expect tile 103
close 103

# Squeezed against a neighbour that has left since, it is squeezed by nobody: everything else is left over.
open Safari 800x600 min 500x300
open Mail 900x600
dock 104 left
dock 105 right
resize 104 right -400
expect tile 104
close 105
expect visible 104
expect size 104 500x851
close 104

# In the Dock when its app is taken out of Arbor's hands: Safari has the room already, and keeps it.
open Safari 900x600
open Mail 900x600
dock 106 left
dock 107 right
minimize 107
expect size 106 1416x851
exclude com.example.mail
expect still 106
expect size 106 1416x851
include com.example.mail
close 106
close 107

# The pointer means what it is seen on. A note that lies behind Safari is not that.
open Safari 900x600
open Mail 900x600
open Notes 300x200
open Music 200x200
move 110 100 100 300 200
move 111 900 500 200 200
dock 108 left
dock 109 right
focus 108
focus 111
cursor 150 150
in
expect fills 108
show-all
# On top of Safari it is.
focus 110
focus 111
cursor 150 150
in
expect camera desktop
